A||||23||Homicidal||What do you guys do when you see another Fiero driver?||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||07-14-2000||12:40 AM||||I usually give the party sign (index and pinky finger in the air, others folded down) and say "YAHHHHHHHHH" as they drive by!<P>Two days ago I fell in love!  A pretty girl driving a white Fiero JUST LIKE MINE, with gorgeous chrome rims!  I wish I was going her direction, but I was turning left.<P>Another I saw today, a nice brilliant blue one, also my model.  once again, I threw the party sign and just said "Yah baby" to myself!<P>But I don't do it to the Fiero owners who own dirty, beat up Fiero's.  They obviously don't appreciate the quality of the car.  <P>The other drivers always smile and wave!  We are connected......||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroGTGirl||07-14-2000||01:12 AM||||Well, Homicidal...<P>For some reason they are always behind me.  I always notice things in my rearview.  Guess I spend to much time looking "behind" me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>So I can't really wave or make eye contact.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GtGirl.JPG"> ||||reg||12
Z||000002||TalShino||07-14-2000||01:16 AM||||Hey now, I drive a dirty beat up Fiero.. but I'm also in the process of fixing it and having very little money and LOTS of time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> but anyways, I saw a 87 White GT the other day... I had to turn around and follow the guy.. he waved, I waved and turned off..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Fiero Owners Unite, We Shall Rise Above It All! hehehehehehehehehe||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||07-14-2000||01:31 AM||||If I'm driving the GT, I hit the "wink" switch, what else  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ?  ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Homicidal||07-14-2000||04:21 AM||||Talshino:  No, the people I see driving them are people you can TELL have no intention of cleaning it up.  Trust me!||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||07-14-2000||06:01 AM||||Usually I open fire to preserve the uniqueness of my car. A few rounds from the sawed-off usually does the trick.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Gokart||07-14-2000||06:44 AM||||Message icon says it all! Then I'll give a quick tap on my air horn <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000007||ChadMan||07-14-2000||09:34 AM||||Usually I just give a quick honk and friendly wave.  But all I gave the last Fiero I saw was a surly glare.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  He had a beautiful white 85 Coupe and was driving 58 mph in the passing lane on the freeway, impeding the flow of morning rush-hour traffic.  His Fiero should be confiscated and given to TalShino.||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||07-14-2000||11:39 AM||||If I see a Fiero ahead of me, usually I'll give the "Fiero Salute", a quick headlights up and down, followed by a smile and a wave. That works quite well. I even do it on the beat up ones, hopefully those who view their Fiero as nothing but transportation will realize the uniqueness of the car when they see someone in another Fiero try to communicate with them. Who knows, maybe they'll take it to the car wash and realize under all that filth, that's a beautiful car!!! <BR>Yesterday a black coupe popped out of no where and got in front of me. I waved and flashed my headlights, with no luck. It finally hit me that I was driving my 2000 Altima! Duhhh! <BR>If I ran across a beautiful, nice woman around my age, 25, that'd be it! I'd be off the market!! LOL||||reg||1
Z||000009||Bruce||07-14-2000||12:10 PM||||I think George is the only one who returned my wave. People in Calif. are too cool and up-tight, I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Majik||07-14-2000||12:28 PM||||I always wave at other fiero owners, but they seldom wave back although some do   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  I do drive a beat up fiero (I'd like to get my hands on the previous owner!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> )  It is in the process of repair and rebuild, but it takes time and money  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   Had a guy in a Mazda flag me down yesterday, his dad blew up his engine in the fiero he just got, and wanted to bs fiero for a bit...man did he find the right guy.<BR>Majik||||reg||6
Z||000011||Black88GT||07-14-2000||01:16 PM||||I very rarely ever pass anything but a crappy 2m4.  However, a couple weeks ago in my GT I saw this hot girl in a white fastback, it might have been an 88 because it was mono paint, but the paint looked great so it probably got repainted.  But anyway, she was driving so fast I couldnt even catch her! She must have thought she was Dale Jarrett or some **** .<P>CRAZY WOMEN DRIVERS!!!!!!||||reg||10
Z||000012||Homicidal||07-14-2000||02:37 PM||||Bruce:  I'm in San Diego and I always get waves back!  Guess you get the sour owners!||||reg||1
Z||000013||WhiteFieroBlur||07-14-2000||03:26 PM||||Man I need to move where ya'll live. I don't ever see any fieros. All I see are old beat up coupe models and no GT models. The only GT I see is mine. I never get a chance to see a real nice fiero pass by. I don't even know what one looks like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I am trying to keep up the fiero over in my town by keeping mine nice and fixing it up. I feel like i am all alone. I am surounded my 200 mustangs and camaros and eclipses who always wanna race. Most people don't even know what car i have in the first place. I get waves and looks alot by people and when a coupe rolls up next to me they don't wave or anything. Probably shocked to see a GT model  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. but as soon as I get my car fixed and painted and looking nice I am sure I'll get more looks than a mustang and camaro could ever get.||||reg||1
Z||000014||TalShino||07-14-2000||05:16 PM||||Hey.. aight.. Donate the Fiero's to me! I'll give em the TLC they need & want.. can't wait to get my baby painted.. though it aint black like I want.. but its just as good  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Hawian Orchid Polly.. yes pics will come asap!!!!!!!||||reg||14
Z||000015||Pontiaddict||07-14-2000||09:17 PM||||I just stare...<BR>or drool...<P>Headlights are up so I can't pop them up and down.<BR>Talshino, HAWAIAN ORCHID???! You could have at  least given a description of the color.||||reg||1
Z||000016||nivlek68||07-15-2000||12:07 AM|||| well i honk and wave seen a nice white coupe in town,she was pretty for a crappy 2m4. mine is a 2m4 thats needs painted but i keep it clean. ||||reg||8
Z||000017||Cliff D.||07-15-2000||12:22 AM||||I can't flash my lights until I get a new multi-function switch because every time I touch the lever, my windshield wipers cycle. If you see a red '85 GT in the Washington DC area that does not use turn signals, please don't get upset. It is embarassing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000018||HYPTNOTiSE||07-15-2000||12:47 AM||||I always try to race them, and i rev my engine. guess it's all this testosterone at a such a young age.  <P>This is funny cos the other day, i was headed to a friends house(already late by the way) and an all black 88 past me. I followed the lady for 12 miles before she pulled over!!! She thought i was crazy. It was so worth it though. She was the original owner of a black 88 GT, which has only been driven weekends and garage kept in between. 31K orignal miles(why does everyone say original miles, like they would be unoriginal or something) Anyway... It has t-tops and an automatic. and leather beechwood interior! It was so pefect and mint. I made her stay there while i drooled.<P><BR>Hey cliff, i live in Frederick, If you ever see a white pearl 86GT going really fast, wave it's prolly me!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000019||TalShino||07-15-2000||01:20 AM||||hmmm.. lets see if I can describe this color, its sorta a LIGHT purple.. it rocks.. You'll see pics when I get em.. maybe I'll hit on over to my friends house and scan ya a pic of my bro's old truck that was painted that color.. it rocked! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000020||Homicidal||07-15-2000||03:33 AM||||I met one guy around the corner from my house, he has an 85 SE.  Paintjob is needed, but the engine is clean and nice.  Runs good but needs an EGR valve.  We plan to head to the junkyard and strip some Fiero's down!||||reg||1
Z||000021||ur2biteme||07-15-2000||08:09 AM||||I'm new to the group, but here in Modesto, CA it's about a 50/50 split of who responds to my eye contact.  <P>It seems like there is an abundance of Fieros in this town.  Even to the extent that they almost never get them in at Pic-n-Pull!  Enough people keeping them on the road here.  I drive delivery in mine and have had 5 pull up at the same light!  <P>Mine is a fairly clean '87 base model, with body damage and problems (i want to strangle the owner previous to me!).  From the condition of most of the parts, it looks like the owner that screwed up the car only had it a short time cuz most of it is like new....modified V6 to be added in a couple years......  <P>my site is at: members.fortunecity.com/ur2biteme/index.htm<BR>i'd like some suggestions.  sorry about the long post.  Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000022||RobertVol||07-16-2000||08:16 PM||||If I'm In the stock GT I give em a little wave and nod. And hit the gas a little! But I always check before I do that..I learned the hard way ....usually when it has wide stance tires and lowered a bit with straight pipes and a tag that says "Eat z28" you DONT mess with it. Oh yeah and the 350 badge kinda should tell you something to! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>In the 3.8 I just fly by the stock GT's give a litle gas and they seem to have this look like YEAH I know!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/0629a880.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000023||FreshAir||07-17-2000||01:37 AM||||I live in Fresno, Ca. And there are plenty of Fieros here.  It is so funny that most people who meet me say "wow, you don't see that many Fieros any more."  A few weeks later they say "those things are all over this town. I can't believe I haven't seen them before."  I have a red/grey '86 SE V-6.  Ususally I try to flash the park lights @ other fieros (horn switch broken by previous owner). I did fly by a beutiful '88 GT w/ dealer plates on Friday.  I was hoping that he would play tag  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
